  - question: "What is DTG t-shirt printing?"
    answer: "DTG means direct to garment. A specialized printer applies textile ink directly to the shirt, allowing detailed, full-color images and smooth tonal changes."
  - question: "What image resolution is best for a photo shirt?"
    answer: "Use the largest, cleanest original you have. The ideal resolution depends on the final print dimensions, so we review the image at its intended size rather than relying on one universal pixel requirement."
  - question: "Which shirts work best for DTG?"
    answer: "Cotton-rich garments are generally the strongest candidates. Shirt weave, color, finish, and blend can affect the printed result, so garment selection is part of the project review."
  - question: "Can the background be removed from my photo?"
    answer: "Background removal may be possible when the subject is clear and the file has enough detail. Share the original image and explain the look you want before the order is finalized."
